title a red costs the receipt -- the roster names what a red close withheld, and the ledger learns that a gate is not a row
prompt the standing INNER LOOP seat -- roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, the council rota, read scope, and the lane's next door
think THE COLD OPEN IS WHAT FOUND THE LAP. `sh tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_run.sh` printed `roster_receipt=none` while `construction/standing-equipment-runs.kyri` beside it held a complete 96-guard pass from `20260830.080600`. Those two readings cannot both be innocent, and reading the runner answered it: the receipt is written at line 570, below the `if [ "$red" -ne 0 ]` branch that exits 1 at line 546. A full pass carrying any red writes no receipt, `--scoped` refuses without one, and this clone's two reds are `pond_enclosure_door` at custody gate %5 and `rule_twin` at gate %7 -- both named on the living card, both parked by a maintainer rather than broken. So the fusion build's cheaper pass is unreachable here by construction, not by delay, and the refusal read `run the full roster once` to a hand who had run it twice that morning at 2h27m a pass.
think THE REPAIR IS ADDITIVE AND MOVES NO GATE, because the receipt's strictness is the whole point -- a scoped close writing one is the road from evidence to rumor the design exists to close. What was missing is not permission but speech: a full pass closing red now prints `roster_receipt_write=withheld_guard_red`, and a `--scoped` without a basis prints `scoped_basis_blocked=<guards>`, read from the run card with eight names then a count, and refuses in a sentence that names them. On this bench it answers `scoped_basis_blocked=pond_enclosure_door,rule_twin`. Whether a receipt may chain from a close whose only reds are custody-gated and card-named loosens what a receipt promises, so it is Keaton's word and is surfaced rather than taken.
think A HYPOTHESIS DIED IN THE PEN BEFORE IT REACHED THE LEDGER. I thought a path-limited `git commit -- <paths>` would drop the pre-commit hook's `git add README.md`, which would have explained the stale front door. A throwaway repository with a page-rewriting hook proved the opposite: the page landed in the commit. What it DOES leave is `MM page.md` -- the main index holding the pre-hook blob while HEAD and the worktree hold the new one -- so a hand tidying that with `git restore --staged` would resurrect the stale page. Measurement beat memory, and the real cause of the stale block was simpler: `b142793a2` cut the last Python file, which dropped the fascia ratchet signal from 2 to 1 and moved the grade 64 to 68 without the page following.
think THE SECOND RED WAS MY OWN ROW BITING A GUARD. `%374` names `gate %5` and `gate %7`, and `reds_status_consistency_scan.sh` reads every `clos(e|es|ed|ing|ure)` and scans 60 characters either side for `%N`, calling each a closure claim. `.claude/rules/git-signing.md` seats `%` for every number this tree assigns itself, so a custody gate and a ledger row wear one sigil and the guard could not tell them apart. Attributed exactly by stashing that single row: `phantom_closures` 0 without it, 2 with it. One `gsub` blanks `gate %N` and `` gate `%N` `` before the token scan, narrow enough that `closed by %N` keeps every tooth. Then the fix's own row bit the same guard again, because I had illustrated it with a real number -- the placeholder law of `.claude/rules/stamp-and-name.md`, arriving one namespace over.
obs FOUR ROSTERED GUARDS STOOD RED AT HEAD ON THIS CLONE, AND THAT IS THE COST OF %374 SPELLED OUT. `nib_honesty` (the card advertised git nib `1399504689`, which `git cat-file -t` refuses), `readme_metrics` (fascia 64 against a fresh 68), `reds_pin_capacity` (`unrecorded_shelves=63` against a ceiling of 62 that only falls), and `reds_status_consistency` once my own row landed. All four were green in the morning pass. Nothing caught them for eleven hours because a full pass costs 2h27m here and the cheaper pass can never be earned.
obs EVERY ONE WAS ATTRIBUTED BEFORE IT WAS REPORTED, by stashing the exact files and re-running. `reds_fold` looked pre-existing and was mine -- the card's Prior-lap row points forward at this very log, so `readme_reach_scan.sh` read one broken living link until the log was written. `reds_pin_capacity` looked mine and was not: today's collision heal landed `REDS-one-number-two-rows-364-371.md` without its recital line, which is the whole of the 62-to-63 rise, and one recital paragraph returns it to 62.
obs THE COLD PASS WAS STOPPED ON PURPOSE AND I SAY SO RATHER THAN LET IT DIE. It had reached 21 of 96 guards when the lap needed to edit the runner, and REDS %221 records that editing the runner mid-run kills the shell. Stopping it deliberately cost the reading and kept the fault; `kill -KILL` left the lock directory behind, which `lock_acquire` reaps by `kill -0` on the next pass, and I cleared it by hand rather than leave the next lap to discover it. The evidence room is written after the close digest, so a stopped pass leaves no evidence files -- the two reds it named were re-run by hand instead.
obs THREE OF FOUR NEW ROSTER READINGS BITE, AND ONE CANNOT, so it is written down as a companion. A runner stripped of both new lines flips `red_close_names_withholding`, `blocked_basis_names_the_guard`, and `unblocked_basis_reads_none` to no; `green_close_names_no_withholding` passes either way, because a stripped runner also prints no withholding. The same honesty holds for the ledger pair: a scan stripped of the gate exemption is STRICTER, so the two narrowness cases pass under the plant and only `gate_reference_free` and `gate_not_a_row` prove the repair.
obs THE ROSTER'S OWN WITNESS CANNOT BE GREEN HERE, WHICH IS %374 ONE LAYER UP. `standing_equipment_witness` refuses at its scan leg for `runs_red=2` on the same two gated rows, so the guard that proves the roster honest is unrunnable on exactly the trees carrying a gate. Its control leg -- including this lap's seven new asserts -- reads GREEN when the witness is run against a card those gates have not reddened, which is how the asserts were proven.
obs THE CARD SITS NINE BYTES UNDER ITS BOUND. Making room for the %374 line meant compressing the settled %360 gate paragraph and retiring the spent `%369` gate block, since `%371` closed that collision this afternoon. At 24,567 of 24,576 the next lap will have to trade a line for a line.
obs ROTA ROW 0, ADVANCED BY HAND. `git rev-list --count HEAD` reads 3844 and 3844 mod 5 is 4, which the previous lap already read, so the aether row was taken instead -- the row that hears, with the compass, the Lindy effect, and the grain. Its own strand says the thing this lap is about: a guard that cannot red guards nothing, and a witness must be proven able to make a sound before its silence means anything. The lap's finding is the next question over -- a guard that CAN red, whose red silently disables a second mechanism that never asked which kind of red it was.
obs THE SEND'S SECOND FETCH FOUND A NUMBER COLLISION, AND THE RULE DECIDED IT WITHOUT A JUDGMENT CALL. `xy/main` had moved one commit while this round was packaged, and that commit booked `%372` and `%373` at `20260830.193555` -- the same two numbers this lap had booked at `20260830.192524` and `20260830.193255`. Earlier stamps lose to earlier LANDING: a published number never moves, mine were unshared, so they derive above the fetched head as `%374` and `%375`. Swept in the rebase across both row headers, five tool comments, the card's Now line, and this log. Fetch-before-book was followed at both bookings and still lost the race, which is `%371`'s own lesson standing unchanged -- the allocator can only answer for what has landed.
obs THE FOUR ROWS TOGETHER CARRIED THE PIN PAST ITS BOUND, so `%359` folded to its own shelf and the recital took the line. `construction/REDS.md` read 26,025 against a declared 24,576 after the rebase merged upstream's two rows beside this lap's two; `equinox_e123_living_pin_guard` is the guard that says so, and `reds_pin_capacity` reads `verdict=ok` beside it, because they measure different things -- capacity reads the trail and the foldable set, the pin guard reads the bytes. Folding the lock row returned the pin to 21,404.
obs THE HOT RE-VERIFY CAUGHT A THIRD PARTY'S BROKEN LINK, WHICH IS THE SAME EVIDENCE AGAIN. Upstream's row on `session-logs/date/README-index-20260830.md` linked `20260830-193650_unheard-sweep-census-30-sidecar.kyri` as a bare filename, without the `20260830/` shelf directory every other row on that page carries, so `readme_reach_scan.sh` read `broken_in_living=1` and `reds_fold` refused. Repointed here in the same round -- references are promises, and a shelf's own index is the one page whose whole job is pointing correctly. It shipped to the anointed remote because the guard that catches it is rostered and nobody on that bench could afford the pass, which is `%374` costing a peer rather than me.
