recommend check-in (Claude) THE WORK IS GREEN AND ONE RULING IS WORTH YOUR WORD. `%374`: the receipt is written past the red exit, so a tree whose reds sit at a custody gate can never earn `--scoped` -- here `pond_enclosure_door` (%5) and `rule_twin` (%7), at 2h27m a full pass, which is why four rostered guards stood red at HEAD for eleven hours today. The diagnosis is honest now and moves no gate; whether a receipt may chain from a close whose ONLY reds are custody-gated and card-named is yours, because it loosens what a receipt promises. `%375` is closed: a gate and a row wear one `%`, and the ledger's guard now reads them apart, proven both ways. Two bench facts unchanged: `standing_equipment_witness` still refuses here at its scan leg for those same two gated rows, and this clone's stale untracked `publish-seed.sh` copy stays named for your hand. Silence's next constructive door is still Comlink's other bounds.
